{"source":"github","project_id":"parsedate","target":"gaborcsardi/parsedate","id":"pr/16","ref":16,"title":"Speed up parse_date for empty input elements","description":"This contributes a drop-in replacement for the current parse_date function. \r\n\r\nI did some benchmarking, and my wrapped implementation provides an up to 1000x speed improvement on sparse vectors:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\u003e microbenchmark(parse_date_fast(l), parse_date(l), times=10)\r\nUnit: milliseconds\r\n               expr         min          lq        mean      median         uq          max neval\r\n parse_date_fast(l)    8.310955    8.498442    8.924408    8.872219    9.15244     9.762069    10\r\n      parse_date(l) 8661.542222 8975.832965 9735.830961 9246.564908 9739.19878 12659.482717    10\r\n\u003e bench \u003c- microbenchmark(parse_date_fast(l), parse_date(l), times=10)\r\n```\r\n\r\nI see a couple of ways how we could implement this, not sure if you like this one best :).\r\n\r\nRefs #15 ","published_at":"2017-02-07T17:33:48Z","updated_at":"2017-02-07T22:11:29Z","url":"https://github.com/gaborcsardi/parsedate/pull/16","type":"pr","extra":{"author":"Inventitech","merged_at":"2017-02-07T22:11:29Z","state":"MERGED"}}
